# Frontend build-time config. Copy to web/.env.local for local overrides, and set
# the same keys in the Vercel project's Environment Variables for a deployment.
#
# Vite only exposes variables prefixed VITE_, and it BAKES THEM INTO THE BUNDLE at
# build time. So: public values only, never a secret, and a change here needs a
# rebuild to take effect - not just a restart.

# Where the token server lives. The console POSTs {user_id, order_id} to
# ${VITE_API_BASE}/livekit-token and gets back a short-lived LiveKit token.
# Leave unset for local development and it falls back to http://localhost:8081.
# Deployed, this must be an HTTPS origin: the page is served over HTTPS and a
# browser will block a plain-HTTP request from it as mixed content.
VITE_API_BASE=https://your-token-server.example
